# Goal: grasp an object at the given pose using the Piper arm and lift it.
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped object_pose
float64 lift_height            # meters; 0.0 means "use the manipulator's configured default"
string object_frame            # TF frame of the object being grasped (e.g. the wall-mount
                               # stage's sensor_cam_N). When set, the manipulator verifies
                               # after CLOSE_GRIPPER that the box is still flat (magnet face
                               # down) -- a grasp-close contact kick rotates it in the
                               # fingers ~30-50% of the time (measured 2026-09-20), and a
                               # rotated box fails wall capture later. Kick -> reopen +
                               # abort so the caller can re-grasp. Empty = check inactive
                               # (legacy pedestal behavior).
---
# Result
bool success
string message
---
# Feedback: stage mirrors the task_coordinator FSM arm states so the
# coordinator never has to duplicate manipulator-internal logic.
# STOW_OBJECT (section 4.16): after LIFT_OBJECT, retracts the arm (still
# holding the object) to the 'zero' SRDF group_state before returning --
# lift_pose alone left the grasped object at roughly the lidar's own
# mount height, in its forward scan cone, which applyObstacleAvoidance()
# (kotek_base_control) then read as "obstacle directly ahead" and zeroed
# forward velocity for the whole DRIVE_TO_DELIVERY leg. 'zero' is the same
# pose retreatToSafe() already uses for failure paths and is confirmed
# clear of the lidar's scan plane.
string stage                   # MOVE_ARM_TO_PREGRASP | MOVE_ARM_TO_GRASP | CLOSE_GRIPPER | LIFT_OBJECT | STOW_OBJECT
float64 progress               # 0.0-1.0 within the current stage
